title: Protect the Leadership
subtitle: The lists of names are already printed in the officers' clubs.
view-if: crisis = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 60
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Protect the Leadership

Nobody has forgotten January 1919. In every crisis, the Freikorps and the political police go looking for the party's leaders first, and they do not always bother with a court.

The Zentrale must decide where its members sleep this week.

- @hide: Hide the leaders in safe houses.
- @openly: Lead openly, in the streets.
- @couriers: Set up a courier network to every district.

@hide
subtitle: The leadership is safe; it is also out of sight.
on-arrival: unity += 3; repression -= 3; crisis_momentum -= 2; lean_luxemburgist += 1

The leaders move every night, from a doctor's flat in Charlottenburg to a gardener's hut in Treptow. The orders still go out, a day late.

@openly
subtitle: The workers see their leaders with them. So do the police.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 4; militancy += 3; repression += 4; unity += 2; offensive_satisfaction += 3; lean_offensive += 1

The Zentrale's members speak from lorries at the factory gates. The crowds roar. Plain-clothes men in the crowd write down the times and places.

@couriers
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The districts hear from the Zentrale every day, and act together.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 5;
}
Q.crisis_momentum += 2;
!}

Young comrades on bicycles and railwaymen with messages in their boots carry the Zentrale's instructions to every district within a day.
